WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.830
PAUL JAY: Welcome back to Reality Asserts
Itself on The Real News Network. I'm Paul

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:12.200
Jay.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.160
We're continuing our series of interviews
with John Kiriakou.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:15.809
Thanks very much for joining us.

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:16.980
JOHN C. KIRIAKOU: Thanks for having me.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.560
JAY: And just to remind everybody, John is
a former CIA officer.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.150
Yes?

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.329
KIRIAKOU: Mhm.

00:00:22.329 --> 00:00:27.430
JAY: And you'll find his whole biography below
here. And I'm hoping you'll watch the earlier

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.160
segments, 'cause this is going to make a heck
of a lot more sense if you have, 'cause we're

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.230
working our way through John's life.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.070
You left Greece. You came back in the year
2000, and you're in Langley. You're working

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:47.410
on Greek terrorism. And then 9/11. So where
are you, and how does it affect you?

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:52.870
KIRIAKOU: I was at CIA headquarters that day.
I was supposed to go to the White House that

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:58.460
morning with Cofer Black, later Ambassador
Cofer Black. Cofer at the time was the director

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.899
of the CIA's Counterterrorism Center. And
we had a meeting scheduled that morning with

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:08.360
Condoleezza Rice, who at the time was the
national security advisor, to discuss a Greek

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:15.360
issue--which seems quaint now, but I had taken
a call from a driver who said that our car

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.430
was ready and to come out to the side entrance
to ride to the White House.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:28.430
JAY: Now, before we do that trip, what's the
mood at CIA? 'Cause we know now, according

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:34.330
to George Tenet, that he had told President
Bush when he--first presidential national

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:38.420
security briefing, that the number-one threat
to the United States was Osama bin Laden and

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:38.790
al-Qaeda.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.549
KIRIAKOU: Yes.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:45.780
JAY: That summer leading up to 9/11, Richard
Clarke says, our hair is on fire. We know

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:52.380
now that there were at least four or five,
and maybe quite a few more, very specific

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.740
pieces of intelligence that suggested there
was going to be an attack. In fact, it was

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.710
even known--some of the people that ended
up on the planes that even had been identified

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:07.299
pre-9/11--there's a lot going on. Now, I know
you're working on the Greek file, but how

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:09.860
much are you getting a sense of this?

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:16.860
KIRIAKOU: Well, I mentioned this in my book.
In July--it was July 6, 2001--I was asked

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:24.230
to spend the day with a visiting group of
Arab intelligence officers. They came to have

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.720
a day of briefings and meetings and handshakes
and gift exchanges. And we did this kind of

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.910
thing all the time with our foreign partners.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:36.690
So, as part of that day of briefings, I had
asked for briefings from the Osama bin Laden

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:43.239
group in the CIA's Counterterrorism Center.
Much to my surprise, they did not send a mid-level

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:47.739
analyst, which is what I had expected, to
do this briefing; Cofer Black himself came.

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:53.239
And Cofer at the time was the director of
the CIA's Counterterrorism Center, then called

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.300
the Counterterrorist Center.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:03:02.110
And Cofer started off this briefing by saying--and
these were his exact words--he said, "something

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:07.300
terrible is going to happen. We don't know
when and we don't know where, but we know

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:13.040
that it's something on an unprecedented scale".
He said, the mood in the al-Qaeda training

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:20.040
camps is one of jubilation. We're hearing
trainers speaking to their students and crying

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:28.090
and saying, I'll see you in paradise. We're
hearing codewords used to describe a major

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:34.080
attack--the salesman is coming with vast quantities
of honey; there's going to be a great soccer

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.489
match; things like that. And he said, we've
never seen anything like this before. Our

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:46.420
problem is we don't know when and we don't
know exactly what the target is. And he said,

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:52.390
I beg you, if you have any sources inside
al-Qaeda, please help us.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:58.140
Well, these guys were silent. I think, frankly,
they were stunned into silence, as I was.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.420
And at the end of the day, after they had
left, I went to his office to thank Cofer

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:07.590
for spending the time doing the briefing.
Again, this was very unusual. And I said to

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:14.330
him, Cofer, I have to ask you, was that for
their benefit, or are things really that bad?

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:19.000
And he said, things really are that bad; we're
going to get hit, and it's going to be terrible.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:26.000
JAY: This is July 2001. Now, we know there
were various sections of the military intelligence

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:35.689
and other areas of various intelligence agencies
that were trying to model what the next attack

00:04:35.689 --> 00:04:36.389
might be.

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:37.029
KIRIAKOU: Yes.

00:04:37.029 --> 00:04:43.020
JAY: One of those models for military intelligence
was planes hitting the Twin Towers. One of

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:49.669
them might even fall down. We did an earlier
report on this. Some investigative journalists--Jason

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:54.619
Leopold, was one of them--actually talked
to one of the guys who was running that unit.

00:04:54.619 --> 00:05:00.449
That information, as far as we know, was suppressed,
in a sense. It may have not made its way up

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:02.979
the food chain, which was rather odd.

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:06.219
Richard Clarke talks about--in fact, did an
interview just a couple of years ago, which

00:05:06.219 --> 00:05:11.020
we also have--we ran on The Real News Network--with
some critical information that never made

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:16.059
it to him. He said that information, in the
normal course of things, would have made it

00:05:16.059 --> 00:05:19.169
to him. Someone had to intervene not to let
it go up the food chain.

00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:25.839
BOB GRAHAM: Fifty--five-oh--CIA personnel
knew about this. You have to intentionally

00:05:25.839 --> 00:05:32.839
stop it. You have to intervene and say, no,
I don't want that report to go. And I never

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.029
got a report to that effect.

00:05:35.029 --> 00:05:42.029
JAY: We asked Senator Bob Graham specifically
about this memo, Osama bin Laden plans to

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:48.080
attack the United States, that no action was
taken after that memo. Now, you get a memo

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:54.069
like that, and you've got the CIA saying something's
coming, how do you not do something?

00:05:54.069 --> 00:05:59.069
KIRIAKOU: I remember Dick Clarke and Cofer
Black both saying that they were shouting

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:06.069
this from the rooftops and no one in the Bush
White House would listen to them.

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:13.319
You're right about the modeling. We knew from
the early 1990s that al-Qaeda was interested

00:06:13.509 --> 00:06:20.509
in using airliners as a weapon. The CIA analysis
at the time was that the attack would probably

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:28.789
be against American embassies again overseas,
because they had such great success doing

00:06:28.789 --> 00:06:29.819
that in the past.

00:06:29.819 --> 00:06:31.199
JAY: Except then you get the memo,--

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:32.020
KIRIAKOU: Right.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.800
JAY: --the memorandum that bin Laden plans
to attack the United States

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.319
KIRIAKOU: Well, we wrote the memo.

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:37.399
JAY: Right. You wrote the memo.

00:06:37.399 --> 00:06:38.300
KIRIAKOU: Yeah, we wrote the memo.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.110
JAY: The CIA writes the memo to, as a presidential
briefing.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:41.610
KIRIAKOU: Yes.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:42.119
JAY: Right.

00:06:42.119 --> 00:06:43.279
KIRIAKOU: Yeah. So we had the memo.

00:06:43.279 --> 00:06:44.479
JAY: So where [crosstalk] information [crosstalk]

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:45.529
KIRIAKOU: Which information's that?

00:06:45.529 --> 00:06:48.749
JAY: That Osama bin Laden plans to attack
United States.

00:06:48.749 --> 00:06:53.129
KIRIAKOU: All-source intelligence. The analysts
were able to put that together. And based

00:06:53.129 --> 00:06:59.289
on these little bits of information that they're
able to pull together, they decided that the

00:06:59.289 --> 00:07:06.050
attack was probably going to be in the United
States, or at least that the intention to

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:10.249
attack was in the United States. We didn't
know that they were already here, because

00:07:10.249 --> 00:07:11.399
the FBI didn't tell us.

00:07:11.399 --> 00:07:13.819
JAY: This is the group in Seattle.

00:07:13.819 --> 00:07:18.309
KIRIAKOU: Well, they were all over the place.
They were in Florida. They were in Washington.

00:07:18.309 --> 00:07:19.360
They were all over the place.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.639
JAY: But the FBI did have knowledge of certain--.

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:22.759
KIRIAKOU: Or at least some of them.

00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:23.149
JAY: Some of them.

00:07:23.149 --> 00:07:23.399
KIRIAKOU: Yeah. Sure

00:07:23.149 --> 00:07:26.599
JAY: I think one in Seattle in particular
turned out to be an FBI informant that had

00:07:26.599 --> 00:07:27.300
two of the people--.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.159
KIRIAKOU: One of the hijackers?

00:07:28.159 --> 00:07:28.809
JAY: No.

00:07:28.809 --> 00:07:30.379
KIRIAKOU: I'm talking about the 19 hijackers.

00:07:30.379 --> 00:07:35.809
JAY: Yeah. Well, two of the hijackers, apparently,
were staying with a guy, a professor, who

00:07:35.809 --> 00:07:40.449
actually had some informant kind of connection
with the FBI, and the FBI didn't tell the

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:41.050
CIA.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:45.539
KIRIAKOU: The FBI's relationship with the
CIA at the time, and really throughout history,

00:07:45.539 --> 00:07:50.719
has been absolutely terrible. We don't like
them, they don't like us. And at least until

00:07:50.719 --> 00:07:57.449
September 11, and probably for some time afterwards,
there really was very, very little cooperation.

00:07:57.449 --> 00:08:01.899
Now, there were FBI agents, certainly, who
were assigned to the CIA's Counterterrorism

00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:06.599
Center, and there were CIA officers assigned
to the FBI's Counterterrorism Center, but

00:08:06.599 --> 00:08:11.080
that didn't necessarily mean that both sides
were seeing all information.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:16.569
JAY: You get a memorandum--and you write a
memorandum; when I say you, I mean the president

00:08:16.569 --> 00:08:22.759
gets a memorandum from the CIA saying Osama
bin Laden plans to attack United States--you

00:08:22.759 --> 00:08:27.830
guys have intelligence at the level that he
tells you and he tells this Arab country's

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:34.070
intelligence officers that something terrible
is coming on a whole new scale. Why do you

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.409
think you cannot get Condoleezza Rice to listen
or the president to listen?

00:08:37.409 --> 00:08:42.870
KIRIAKOU: So this is one of the enduring mysteries
of the Bush administration. I don't know why

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:49.870
the Bush White House was not focused solely
on trying to stop this attack.

00:08:50.259 --> 00:08:50.629
JAY: [crosstalk]

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:51.649
KIRIAKOU: We all knew what was coming.

00:08:51.649 --> 00:08:53.690
JAY: --seemed to be making efforts not to
want to know.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:54.930
KIRIAKOU: It kind of seems that way.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:59.660
JAY: I mean, how do you get--Coleen Rowley's
group in Minneapolis can't get a warrant to

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.019
go into a computer of a guy that wants to
learn how to take off and not [crosstalk]

00:09:03.019 --> 00:09:03.870
KIRIAKOU: And not land.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:09.420
JAY: I mean, this is--how do you demote Richard
Clarke? How do you have a briefing by the

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:09.670
CIA,--

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.350
KIRIAKOU: And they did.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:14.800
JAY: --who tells you the number-one problem's
al-Qaeda, and you demote your antiterrorism

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.170
czar?

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.050
KIRIAKOU: That's a good question.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.120
JAY: How do you tell--apparently, the FBI
was told, don't focus on terrorism; we want

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.129
you to focus on white-collar crime or something
else.

00:09:25.129 --> 00:09:29.629
KIRIAKOU: Right. There was an article just
in the paper saying that the FBI is still

00:09:29.629 --> 00:09:35.300
unequipped to handle counterterrorism cases.
Nobody there speaks Arabic, for example. They're

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.459
still not focused.

00:09:36.459 --> 00:09:42.009
JAY: Well, I guess what I'm suggesting is
that--not suggesting--there seems to be actual

00:09:42.009 --> 00:09:46.940
real evidence, hard evidence, that it's not
a lack of focus; they were told not to focus.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:47.899
KIRIAKOU: By whom? Who does the--.

00:09:47.899 --> 00:09:52.720
JAY: By the White House. The White House is
telling the FBI to deprioritize terrorism.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.069
They demote Richard Clarke. And then Richard
Clarke's screaming he can't get their attention

00:09:57.069 --> 00:10:02.920
when his hair is on fire. I mean, this is--I
asked Senator Graham this. Well, what do you

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:09.269
think? Is this, like, a deliberate culture
created to not know what's coming? And here's

00:10:09.269 --> 00:10:10.000
what he said.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:16.009
GRAHAM: The fact that it was so pervasive
that virtually all of the agencies of the

00:10:16.009 --> 00:10:23.009
federal government were moving in the same
direction, from a customs agent at an airport

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:30.660
in Orlando who was chastised when he denied
entry into the United States to a Saudi, to

00:10:31.459 --> 00:10:38.459
the president of the United States authorizing
large numbers of Saudis to leave the country,

00:10:39.189 --> 00:10:46.189
possibly denying us forever important insights
and information on what happened. You don't

00:10:47.329 --> 00:10:54.329
have everybody moving in the same direction
without there being a head coach somewhere

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:59.420
who is giving them instructions as to where
he wants them to move.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:03.240
JAY: So that includes before and after the
events.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:10.240
GRAHAM: Primarily before the event. After
the event, it shifts from being an action

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:18.170
that supports the activities of the Saudis
to actions that cover up the results of that

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.930
permission given to the Saudis to act.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:28.600
JAY: There's got to be a coach. The coach
is in the White House. He didn't say Dick

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:28.990
Cheney,--

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:29.779
KIRIAKOU: Right.

00:11:29.779 --> 00:11:34.430
JAY: --but one can--he's not leaving, you
know, much difficulty trying to understand

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:35.509
what he's trying to say here.

00:11:35.509 --> 00:11:41.610
What do you think? Was there a deliberate
leaving the back door open?

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:45.720
And let me put one more little piece of context.
We know in the Project for a New American

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:51.509
Century this document that a lot of neocons
signed in the 1990s, which called, essentially,

00:11:51.509 --> 00:11:56.610
for the assertion of American military power
around the world to reshape the world. And

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:01.449
it even goes--it goes so far as to say international
law was, like, useful when there was another

00:12:01.449 --> 00:12:07.060
superpower, but now it's not really so necessary
anymore, international law. We need to do

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:13.009
the regime changes we need. But they say we'll
never get the American people behind us, because

00:12:13.009 --> 00:12:18.730
there's still the Vietnam syndrome, and only
another galvanizing event--I may not be quoting

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:24.779
it exactly, but it's pretty close--galvanizing
event like another Pearl Harbor would create

00:12:24.779 --> 00:12:28.930
public support for this kind of a foreign
policy.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:35.930
Then we get what seems like evidence that
they don't want the agencies to know.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:40.649
KIRIAKOU: I don't know, to be honest with
you. I can speculate.

00:12:40.649 --> 00:12:46.870
I can tell you that the war game model showing
an attack with an airplane was one of hundreds,

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:52.540
hundreds of models. To be able to pick out
one model and say this is the one that it's

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.779
going to be I think was probably impossible.

00:12:54.779 --> 00:13:01.779
I can tell you, in the CIA I never saw people
work so hard in my entire life trying to disrupt

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:08.860
this attack, and having not enough information
and nowhere near the budget necessary to really

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:10.110
do it.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:14.449
JAY: And doing it in spite of the White House,--

00:13:14.449 --> 00:13:14.759
KIRIAKOU: Yeah.

00:13:14.759 --> 00:13:15.389
JAY: --in a sense,--

00:13:15.389 --> 00:13:15.699
KIRIAKOU: Yeah.

00:13:15.699 --> 00:13:18.779
JAY: --because the White House is not listening
to their own CIA director.

00:13:18.779 --> 00:13:21.930
KIRIAKOU: They're not listening, they're not
cooperating, and they're offering appropriate

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:22.350
funding.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:27.850
Now, Dick Clarke, Dick Clarke was a hero of
the Clinton administration, but I think that

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:34.850
when the George W. Bush people came into power,
they saw this guy that's been in the same

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:42.160
position for ten years, he's gay, he's a liberal
Democrat; it's time to give him the heave-ho.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.749
JAY: So why not give him the heave-ho?

00:13:43.749 --> 00:13:45.360
KIRIAKOU: And they demoted him.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:49.639
JAY: No, no, no. Why not give him the heave-ho
and put someone else at the same level, with

00:13:49.639 --> 00:13:53.290
cabinet-level access, and put in somebody
you like who--I mean, it doesn't have to be

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:53.829
Richard Clarke.

00:13:53.829 --> 00:13:58.079
KIRIAKOU: Well, Condi Rice took it over. It
was supposed to be Condi Rice's responsibility,

00:13:58.079 --> 00:13:58.540
counterterrorism.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:02.279
JAY: Well, she's not even listening to the
people who are doing the work.

00:14:02.279 --> 00:14:04.509
KIRIAKOU: Well, that's on Condi Rice, isn't
it?

00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:05.779
JAY: Well, partly.

00:14:05.779 --> 00:14:06.629
KIRIAKOU: Yeah.

00:14:06.629 --> 00:14:10.839
JAY: But as I'm saying, there seems to be
a pattern here. It's not like--it's not just

00:14:10.839 --> 00:14:11.610
some series of--.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:15.230
KIRIAKOU: I wouldn't call it hard evidence,
though, like you do. I would call it some

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.309
circumstantial evidence.

00:14:16.309 --> 00:14:18.389
JAY: There's certainly enough evidence that
it should be looked into, wouldn't one think?

00:14:18.389 --> 00:14:22.879
KIRIAKOU: Yeah, I would think so. Sure. But
who in Congress has the balls to even take

00:14:22.879 --> 00:14:25.809
something like this up? It's just not going
to happen.

00:14:25.809 --> 00:14:29.809
JAY: No, it's not. But the media doesn't have
the balls either.

00:14:29.809 --> 00:14:31.939
KIRIAKOU: Well, the media doesn't have the
balls, no.

00:14:31.939 --> 00:14:36.920
JAY: After we interviewed Bob Graham, agree
or disagree, Bob Graham is an insider.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:37.240
KIRIAKOU: Absolutely.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.999
JAY: Bob Graham is a serious intelligence
guy.

00:14:39.999 --> 00:14:42.149
KIRIAKOU: Yes, he is. Highly respected.

00:14:42.149 --> 00:14:47.569
JAY: After he leaves the Senate, after he
writes this book saying the number-one reason

00:14:47.569 --> 00:14:52.649
to impeach George Bush is 'cause he didn't
stop 9/11 when he could have--that's in Graham's

00:14:52.649 --> 00:14:58.949
book--after he says that the Saudis are directly
involved--I mean, he says all these things,

00:14:58.949 --> 00:15:03.480
and Leon Panetta appoints him to the external
advisory committee of the CIA.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:03.779
KIRIAKOU: Right.

00:15:03.779 --> 00:15:04.850
JAY: Like, he's not a marginal--.

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:06.749
KIRIAKOU: No, no. He's a serious guy. Right.

00:15:06.749 --> 00:15:11.730
JAY: A serious guy. So I do this interview
with Graham, and he says all the football

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:15.050
players running in the same direction, and
we're talking about the American intelligence

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:22.050
agencies not being able to pursue what they
find is evidence of a growing plan to attack

00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:29.769
America, he says there is a coach. That's
news, right? We send this out to all the news

00:15:29.769 --> 00:15:34.990
organizations up and down the United States.
As a release, we offer them the footage for

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:41.990
free. We give them a transcript of the key
sections. Not a single news agency or a newspaper

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:46.019
even calls us to find out what we have.

00:15:46.019 --> 00:15:52.300
KIRIAKOU: That's the story of the mainstream
media in this country. They're just not interested

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.629
in deep, investigative, serious reporting.

00:15:55.629 --> 00:16:02.629
JAY: I mean, I have to say, I think part of
it is is this stuff about the buildings coming

00:16:02.689 --> 00:16:06.910
down and, you know, explosives and various
thermal--.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.399
KIRIAKOU: Yeah, I don't believe any of that.

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:13.490
JAY: I think it's actually--you know, I've
told people that believe this stuff, you know,

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:17.199
if 50 years or 100 years from now you turn
out to be right, I actually still think you

00:16:17.199 --> 00:16:22.829
should shut up right now, because there's
a real conspiracy--there's at least some verifiable

00:16:22.829 --> 00:16:29.100
evidence that there might have actually been
a deliberate attempt to mess with the intelligence

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:34.610
agencies and leave the back door open. There's
at least enough--what's it called?--prima

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:38.910
facie to look into it. And the stuff about
the building just kind of freaked everyone

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:44.019
out so much that it seems so absurd. And even
if it turns out it's true, it gets in the

00:16:44.019 --> 00:16:48.490
way of something that is actually there and
verifiable.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:49.420
KIRIAKOU: Mhm. Mhm. Something important.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:55.399
JAY: Well, rather important--it's 9/11. If
the thing is--if there is a certain kind of

00:16:55.399 --> 00:16:59.449
collaboration, and if it is with the Saudis,
which is what Bob Graham's committee concludes,

00:16:59.449 --> 00:17:05.260
that the Saudi government is directly involved
in, in their words facilitating--or Graham's

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:08.500
words, facilitating and funding, then--.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:15.500
KIRIAKOU: See, I never saw that. I saw Saudi
individuals who--some of whom had ties to

00:17:16.779 --> 00:17:22.390
the Saudi government or the Saudi royal family,
but I never saw this as a Saudi conspiracy.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:29.390
JAY: He says so. He says the committee reached
that conclusion.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:35.210
My own take, having interviewed quite a few
people that know the Saudi governmental structure,

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:38.470
they describe it more like a feudal structure,
in a sense, that there's--

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:38.880
KIRIAKOU: It is.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.240
JAY: --many power centers.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:45.370
KIRIAKOU: Sure--well, no. There aren't many
power centers. There's one made power center,

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.309
and that's the king. He's an absolute ruler.

00:17:48.309 --> 00:17:53.130
But there are influential people around the
country, and their influence is based on the

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:58.179
amount of money that they have. That's been
going on since oil was discovered in Saudi

00:17:58.179 --> 00:17:59.090
Arabia.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:04.770
JAY: So you can imagine that something like
this can happen without coming directly from

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:05.649
the king.

00:18:05.649 --> 00:18:09.460
KIRIAKOU: Absolutely. Absolutely. I mean,
look at the bin Laden family. The bin Laden

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:16.390
family, it's a highly respected, old family
in Saudi Arabia, originally from Yemen. The

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:23.220
old man bin Laden was worth billions of dollars,
and it was because he was the country's greatest

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:27.840
construction magnate, and not just for Saudi
Arabia, but first all over the peninsula,

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:32.200
and then really throughout the Middle East.
If you wanted something built--an airport,

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:39.200
a port, hospitals, hotels--it was bin Laden
that did it. No, the bin Ladens have absolutely

00:18:40.299 --> 00:18:47.299
no blood ties to the royal family. They don't
even have any marital ties to the royal family.

00:18:47.399 --> 00:18:50.470
But the bin Ladens are a force to be reckoned
with in Saudi Arabia.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:57.470
I think it was people who had bin Laden kind
of money who were involved in funding and

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:02.980
financing al-Qaeda. It wasn't necessarily
the Saudi government. It wasn't necessarily

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:07.380
even members of the Saudi Royal family, although
there probably were a couple of rogues. I

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:13.700
think it was these wealthy businessmen who
really keep the country humming, at least

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:18.260
keep its non-oil economy humming. They were
the ones we should have been looking at.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:24.789
JAY: I have no idea who's right in this, but
it is beyond belief, is it not, that there

00:19:24.789 --> 00:19:30.080
has never been an investigation into what's
in those 28 pages, the 28 redacted pages of

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.950
the joint congressional investigation.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.279
KIRIAKOU: Absolutely.

00:19:34.279 --> 00:19:41.000
JAY: Graham, without ambiguity, says the word
government. And in the interview I stress

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:46.179
it by saying government. He says the government.
I said, not some rogue princes or something?

00:19:46.179 --> 00:19:51.230
He says, no, government. He says they have
hard intelligence, and that it's in the 28

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:53.789
pages, and he's not allowed to say what's
in the 28 pages.

00:19:53.789 --> 00:19:56.360
KIRIAKOU: I never saw any such intelligence.
Never.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.429
JAY: But you weren't in that section.

00:19:58.429 --> 00:20:02.990
KIRIAKOU: But I spent most of my career working
on Saudi Arabia in one way or another, and

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.000
I just never saw anything like that.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:09.070
JAY: Okay. Alright. We're going to continue
our discussion with John. We're going to pick

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:16.070
up where he was on 9/11 and the atmosphere
in CIA and his role. And he ends up in Pakistan.

00:20:18.649 --> 00:20:25.649
Please join us for the continuation of Reality
Asserts Itself on The Real News Network.

